%% Slow oscillation detection and propagation analysis
% This script preprocesses NREM thalamic EEG data by excluding bad channels,
% normalizing the remaining signals, and filtering them between 0.5 and 4 Hz
% for slow oscillation (SO) detection. SO events are detected across channels,
% and the channel with the highest number of SOs is selected as the reference.
% Inter-channel SO delays and peak-amplitude ratios are calculated from the
% mean signal and reference channel and compared between 0.5–4 Hz and
% 0.5–10 Hz filtering ranges. The resulting SO measures and figures are saved
% for subsequent analysis.

